---
title: "Columns Tool Panel - Configuration"
enterprise: true
---

Configure the Columns Tool Panel through `toolPanelParams`: show and hide its sections and columns, control the column order, and prevent changes to grouping, aggregation and pivoting.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Tool Panel Simple" name="simple"  exampleHeight=630 /%}

The example above shows the Columns Tool Panel with its default configuration, `sideBar: 'columns'`. Note the following:

- Columns can only be dragged into the Row Groups, Values and Column Labels sections when their column definition allows it, using `enableRowGroup`, `enableValue` and `enablePivot` respectively.
- The athlete, age, country, year, date and sport columns set `enableRowGroup` and `enablePivot`, so they can be dragged to the Row Groups and Column Labels sections.
- The medal columns set `enableValue`, so they can be dragged to the Values section.

## Tool Panel Parameters

The Columns section and the [Column Chooser](./column-chooser/) use the same column selection panel. Their shared options are defined by `IColumnSelectionPanelParams`, while `IToolPanelColumnCompParams` adds options for the other Columns Tool Panel sections. See [Providing Parameters to Tool Panels](./side-bar/#providing-parameters-to-tool-panels) for how to pass these to the tool panel.

### Shared Column Selection Options

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="IColumnSelectionPanelParams" config={"overrideBottomMargin":"1rem"} /%}

### Columns Tool Panel Options

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="IToolPanelColumnCompParams" names=["suppressColumnMove", "suppressRowGroups", "suppressValues", "suppressPivots", "suppressPivotMode", "buttons"] config={"overrideBottomMargin":"1rem"} /%}

## Section Visibility

Use the following parameters to remove sections from the Columns Tool Panel:

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="IToolPanelColumnCompParams" names=["suppressPivotMode", "suppressRowGroups", "suppressValues", "suppressPivots"] config={"description":"", "overrideBottomMargin":"1rem"} /%}

Use the following parameters to remove controls from the top area:

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="IColumnSelectionPanelParams" names=["suppressColumnExpandAll", "suppressColumnSelectAll", "suppressColumnFilter"] config={"description":"", "overrideBottomMargin":"1rem"} /%}

To show or hide sections after the grid is created, call `setPivotModeSectionVisible()`, `setRowGroupsSectionVisible()`, `setValuesSectionVisible()` or `setPivotSectionVisible()` on the [Columns Tool Panel instance](./tool-panel-columns-layout/#columns-tool-panel-instance). The top area controls have no equivalent methods.

The example below hides all of these sections and controls with the parameters above. Note the following:

- The **Pivot Mode**, **Row Groups**, **Values** and **Column Labels** checkboxes show and hide each section using the methods above.
- The Expand / Collapse All, Select / Unselect All and Search controls stay hidden, as they can only be set through `toolPanelParams`.
- The date column is hidden from the tool panel; see [Hiding Columns](#hiding-columns).

{% gridExampleRunner title="Section Visibility" name="section-visibility"  exampleHeight=630 /%}

## Hiding Columns

To remove a column from the tool panel, set `suppressColumnsToolPanel` on its column definition. This is useful for a column that works in the background, such as one the grid groups by, that users should not see.

{% apiDocumentation source="column-properties/properties.json" section="columns" names=["suppressColumnsToolPanel"] /%}

## Suppress Column Reordering

By default, reordering columns in the grid also reorders them in the Columns section. Set `suppressSyncLayoutWithGrid` to keep the tool panel order fixed.

Users can also reorder columns by dragging them within the Columns section. Set `suppressColumnMove` to prevent this.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    sideBar: {
        toolPanels: [
            {
                id: 'columns',
                labelDefault: 'Columns',
                labelKey: 'columns',
                iconKey: 'columns',
                toolPanel: 'agColumnsToolPanel',
                toolPanelParams: {
                    // tool panel columns won't move when columns are reordered in the grid
                    suppressSyncLayoutWithGrid: true,
                    // prevents columns being reordered from the Columns Tool Panel
                    suppressColumnMove: true,
                },
            },
        ],
        defaultToolPanel: 'columns',
    },
}
```

The two properties are usually enabled together, but can be set independently.

The example below enables both properties. Note the following:

- Moving columns in the grid doesn't reorder columns in the Columns Tool Panel, as `suppressSyncLayoutWithGrid=true`.
- Columns can't be reordered from the Columns Tool Panel, as `suppressColumnMove=true`.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Suppress Column Reordering" name="suppress-column-reordering"  exampleHeight=670 /%}

## Custom Column Layout

By default, the Columns section follows the order of `columnDefs` and stays in sync as columns move in the grid. To define a different layout, pass [Column Definitions](./column-definitions/) to `setColumnLayout()` on the [Columns Tool Panel instance](./tool-panel-columns-layout/#columns-tool-panel-instance).

Given these column definitions supplied to the grid:

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    columnDefs: [
        { field: 'a' },
        { field: 'b' },
        { field: 'c' }
    ]
}
```

The following layout adds a group, reorders the columns and omits column `b`:

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const columnsToolPanel = api.getToolPanelInstance('columns');

columnsToolPanel.setColumnLayout([
    {
        headerName: 'Group 1', // group doesn't appear in grid
        children: [
            { field: 'c' }, // custom column order with column "b" omitted
            { field: 'a' }
        ]
    }
]);
```

The layout can contain column groups that don't exist in the grid, and can omit or reorder columns, but every column it references must already exist in the grid.

{% note %}
When providing a custom layout, enable both `suppressSyncLayoutWithGrid` and `suppressColumnMove` (see [Suppress Column Reordering](#suppress-column-reordering)).
{% /note %}

The example below shows two custom layouts for the Columns Tool Panel. Note the following:

- When the grid is initialised, the Columns Tool Panel layout matches `gridOptions.columnDefs`.
- **Custom Sort Layout** calls `setColumnLayout(colDefs)` with the columns in ascending order.
- **Custom Group Layout** calls `setColumnLayout(colDefs)` with column groups that don't appear in the grid.
- Moving columns in the grid doesn't affect the custom layouts, as `suppressSyncLayoutWithGrid` is enabled.
- Moving columns within the Columns Tool Panel is disabled, as `suppressColumnMove` is enabled.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Custom Column Layout" name="custom-layout"  exampleHeight=640 /%}

## Read Only Functions

Set the grid option `functionsReadOnly=true` to prevent users changing grouping, pivoting or aggregation through the UI. The Row Groups, Values and Column Labels sections stay visible, so users can see which columns are in use but cannot change them.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Read Only Example" name="read-only"  exampleHeight=670 /%}
